.TH PCWEBADB 1 "2026-11-15" "pcwebadb 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pcwebadb \- desktop ADB device manager inspired by sky adb
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcwebadb
.RI [ \-port\  PORT ]
.RI [ \-adb\  PATH ]
.RI [ \-window\  MODE ]
.RI [ \-no\-browser ]
.RI [ \-headless ]
.RI [ \-new\-instance ]
.RI [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PC Web ADB (PWA)
is a Linux desktop ADB client whose feature set and interaction model follow
the GPL\-3.0 Android application
.B sky adb
(github.com/sky22333/skyadb).
.PP
By default it opens a standalone GTK3 window with an embedded WebKitGTK view:
a normal application window with its own title bar and dock entry, no address
bar and no browser tabs. Closing the window does NOT terminate the process:
the window is hidden, the service keeps running in the background and a
notification-area (system tray) icon appears. Left-clicking the icon or
choosing "show main window" restores the window; only the tray's "quit" item,
a termination signal or system shutdown stops the service. The loopback HTTP
endpoint is an internal transport between the Go backend and that embedded
view; it is bound to 127.0.0.1, checks the Host header and is never exposed
to the LAN. A second GUI launch detects the running instance with
.BR flock (2)
and raises the existing window instead of starting a second service; this is
also the recovery path on desktops that hide the system tray.
.PP
GTK3 and WebKitGTK are loaded with
.BR dlopen (3)
at runtime. If they are unavailable, the program falls back to a Chromium
or Firefox
.B --app
style standalone window, then to the default browser, and finally to a
service-only mode. None of these libraries is a hard link-time dependency.
.PP
Features include wireless\-debugging pairing and connection, LAN device
discovery, recent devices, device information, application management,
remote file browsing and transfer, screenshots, logcat, ADB shell, a
virtual remote control, screen mirroring through
.BR scrcpy (1),
diagnostics and preferences.
.PP
An official Android SDK Platform Tools
.B adb
binary is bundled, so Android 11+ wireless pairing works without installing
.B android\-sdk\-platform\-tools
separately. Settings and recent devices are stored in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pcwebadb/config.json .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-port " PORT"
Listen on a fixed loopback port instead of an automatically chosen one.
.TP
.BI \-adb " PATH"
Use a specific adb executable. Also honours the
.B SKYADB_ADB
environment variable and the "custom adb path" setting.
.TP
.BI \-window " MODE"
Select the Linux desktop shell.
.B auto
(the default) tries the native GTK/WebKit window, then a standalone browser
window, then service-only mode;
.B gtk
requires the native window;
.B browser
starts a chrome-less Chromium/Firefox application window;
.B none
starts no UI at all.
.TP
.B \-headless
Alias for
.BR \-window=none .
.TP
.B \-no\-browser
Do not open any UI; print the URL to the terminal and keep serving until
Ctrl+C. Kept for compatibility with earlier releases.
.TP
.B \-new\-instance
Skip the single-instance check and start an independent service on a separate
port. Useful for debugging or running several fixed-port services at once.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKYADB_ADB
Override the adb executable path.
.TP
.B SKYADB_BROWSER
Override the fallback browser command used in
.B \-window=browser
mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/pcwebadb/adb
Bundled Android SDK Platform Tools adb 37.0.1.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/pcwebadb.desktop
Desktop launcher (StartupWMClass=PCWebADB).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pcwebadb/
config.json (settings and recent devices), instance.lock / instance.addr
(single-instance coordination) and tray\-icon.png (notification-area icon).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/pcwebadb/
copyright, changelog, README.Debian, NOTICE.txt and source.tar.gz.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1),
.BR scrcpy (1)
